    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Remember the Panch Prayag confluences: Vishnuprayag, Nandaprayag, Karnaprayag, Rudraprayag, and Devprayag.",
        "West-flowing rivers like Narmada and Tapi form estuaries instead of deltas due to high speed and rift valley beds.",
        "Majuli on the Brahmaputra River in Assam is recognized as the world's largest riverine island.",
        "Mahi River is the only river in India that cuts the Tropic of Cancer twice."
      ],
